---
description: Run pre-commit before committing Python or docs changes
globs:
  - "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

Before `git commit`, run the full pre-commit suite (same as CI):

```bash
bash scripts/pre-commit-check.sh
```

Or commit via:

```bash
bash scripts/git-commit.sh -m "message"
```

After cloning, run `bash scripts/setup-git-hooks.sh` once so `git commit` invokes `.githooks/pre-commit` automatically.

Do not use `git commit --no-verify` to skip hooks unless the user explicitly requests it.
